abstract="We develop a polarised variant of Curien and Herbelin's {\$}{\backslash}bar{\{}{\backslash}lambda{\}}{\backslash}mu{\backslash}tilde{\{}{\backslash}mu{\}}{\$}calculus suitable for sequent calculi that admit a focalising cut elimination (i.e. whose proofs are focalised when cut-free), such as Girard's classical logic LC or linear logic. This gives a setting in which Krivine's classical realisability extends naturally (in particular to call-by-value), with a presentation in terms of orthogonality. We give examples of applications to the theory of programming languages.",
